Purpose: Address and credit card autofill keeps one storage for the whole profile, so a record saved in one container is offered in every container. With the new pref extensions.formautofill.isolate_by_user_context (default false, so Firefox is unchanged) FormAutofillParent serves each page from the storage of its container (userContextId), kept in autofill-profiles-<id>.json beside the default one; the saved-field-names gate is the union over all containers. A second pref, extensions.formautofill.prompterModuleURI, names the module that asks whether to save a captured record, for applications without Firefox's doorhanger UI. Upstreamable: the per-container storage yes, behind the pref; the prompter hook is a small seam.
Test: MOZCONFIG=swell/mozconfig ./mach test swell/tests/app/isolation/browser/browser_autofill.js --headless

